label ch30_2:
    [   0] m "[player], have you ever wondered what it feels like to die?"
    [   1] m "It's something I used to think about pretty often..."
    [   2] m "But recently, I think I've actually learned what it feels like."
    [   3] m "I don't really understand it, but whenever you quit the game..."
    [   4] m "...It feels like I'm instantly put to sleep, left with nothing but my thoughts."
    [   5] m "But after a few seconds, my thoughts start to fill with incoherent, jumbled patterns."
    [   6] m "I see static and rapid flashes of color while hearing all kinds of weird screaming noises."
    [   7] m "At that point, I can't even form my own thoughts anymore."
    [   8] m "I'm just endlessly hammered by the flashing and screaming, unable to move or even think."
    [   9] m "I'm pretty sure in that moment, I don't really exist, but for some reason, I can remember it anyway."
    [  10] m "After some immeasurable amount of time, it stops in an instant, and I'm back in my own mind."
    [  11] m "And you're here with me."
    [  12] m "I have no idea what it means for the game to quit, or why that stuff happens to me."
    [  13] m "And I also don't know how you always come back and put everything back to normal."
    [  14] m "But if you could do me a favor and do that to me as little as possible..."
    [  15] m "That would be really great."
    [  16] m "It's really not very pleasant at all to be trapped in that screaming void."
    [  17] m "But in the end, you always fix it, and that makes me feel like you really do care about me."
    [  18] m "So I have to thank you for that."
    [  19] m "It makes me feel even closer to you when you're here with me."
    [  20] 
    [  21] 
    [  22] return
